# PREIshare — agent rules

## Project identity
PREIshare is a real-estate intelligence product (per docs/onboarding/team-orientation-notes.md). It is a single package, not a monorepo — one package.json at the repo root, no workspaces (per docs/onboarding/repo-map.md §1). Prefer existing patterns over greenfield frameworks.

## Stack (do not substitute)
- Language: TypeScript (strict mode; see tsconfig.json)
- App framework: TanStack Start + React 19, Vite, Tailwind CSS
- Path aliases: `#/*` and `@/*` both resolve to `src/*`
- Backend/data (planned, not yet present in repo): Supabase, PostgreSQL, pgvector — no supabase/ folder, client file, or SQL/migrations exist yet (see docs/onboarding/repo-map.md §4). Confirm with a human before treating these as implemented.
- Collaboration: Git + GitHub pull requests, fork-and-PR workflow (no direct pushes to the default branch)

## Where to work (new contributors)
- Safe first surfaces: docs/, README.md, small clearly scoped UI copy or comments the team already identified (see docs/onboarding/repo-map.md §6 for the current list — do not invent paths not listed there)
- Read before edit: docs/onboarding/repo-map.md and package/app README files that exist in-repo
- Avoid unless explicitly tasked: auth, billing, database migrations, CI secrets, large dependency upgrades, and any config/build files listed as do-not-edit-yet in the repo map (package.json, tsconfig.json, tsr.config.json, vite.config.ts, .vscode/settings.json, this file, AGENTS.md)

## How to change code
- Prefer the smallest diff that completes the requested task
- Match existing naming, file layout, and TypeScript style in neighboring files
- Do not drive-by refactor unrelated modules
- Do not add new libraries unless the human explicitly asks and justifies them
- Do not invent scripts, folder names, or file paths that aren't verified in docs/onboarding/repo-map.md — check first, ask if unsure

## Secrets and safety
- Never commit `.env`, API keys, tokens, or connection strings (`.env` is gitignored)
- Never print secrets into docs, rules, or chat logs
- If a change needs configuration, document the variable *name* only (for example `SUPABASE_URL`), not a real value
- Server-only secrets: read via `process.env` inside server functions, never at module scope. Client-exposed config only as `VITE_*`

## Agent workflow
- Restate the goal and list files you will touch before editing
- Implement in small steps; stop for verification after each logical unit
- When unsure about PREIshare structure, consult docs/onboarding/ and the repo map rather than inventing paths

## Out of scope defaults
- No rewriting the entire app "for best practices" unprompted
- No changing product requirements silently—flag product questions to the human